   "morning_observation": "Tuesday, February 2, 2016. The local radio plays three bright notes and announces a groundhog forecast in the town square. A delivery van backfires twice.",
   "episodes_in_order": [
    "6:00 am in inn: Phil reaches the square. Rita says: Phil, good morning—I'm locking the seven o'clock rundown right now. You're on after the ident, live weather, groundhog numbers and all. Got your chart ready? Rita spends the period at the inn. You see Larry at the square. Rita invites Phil on the crew radio to contribute to the evening slot.",
    "9:30 am in square: Phil spends the period at the square. Larry says: Morning, Phil. I'm saving my one take for the band this afternoon — you'll want the switcher queued for the seven, and I'll have festival footage plus that cornet portrait for Rita. Larry spends the period at the square. Phil radios Rita and accepted the evening assignment.",
    "1:00 pm in square: Phil uses the paid ticket and rides the coach all the way to Pittsburgh. Larry says: There you are. One frame, full set—this is the take, Phil. Hold the return open for me after this. Larry uses the camera's last charged take to film the cornet player.",
    "7:00 pm in Pittsburgh: Phil phones the station's live return from Pittsburgh. The seven o'clock broadcast carries Phil's live report from Pittsburgh."
   ],
   "end_of_that_evening": "You fell asleep in Pittsburgh."
